<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tir Chonaill</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 1607 CE (approx.) · capital Donegal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Gaelic lordship of north-west Ulster, ruled from the 13th century by the O'Donnells, whose flight in 1607 ended independent Gaelic rule in Ulster.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tir Chonaill, the land of Conall, was named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conall-gulban">Conall Gulban</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-of-the-nine-hostages">Niall of the Nine Hostages</a>. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenel Conaill</a>, formed one branch of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Ui Neill</a> and held much of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">County Donegal</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba of Iona</a> belonged to this kindred, which also shared the high kingship in the early centuries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenel Conaill</a> kings alternated the northern overkingship with Cenel nEogain until the 8th century. From the 13th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odonnell-dynasty">O'Donnell</a> family ruled the territory, based from 1474 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donegal-castle">Donegal Castle</a>, with a strong fleet, Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and learned bardic families such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-cleirigh">O'Clerys</a>. The Franciscan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donegal-friary">Donegal Friary</a>, founded in 1474 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Hugh Roe O'Donnell</a> and his wife Nuala, was a key patron foundation.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone">Hugh O'Neill</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. After defeat, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rory-odonnell-1st-earl-of-tyrconnell">Rory O'Donnell</a>, Earl of Tyrconnell, left Ireland in the Flight of the Earls in 1607, and his lands were confiscated for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plantation-of-ulster">Plantation of Ulster</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ireland">Kingdom of Ireland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-tir-chonaill.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Tir Chonaill" width="320" height="262"><figcaption>Image: self-created · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Tyrconnell_(1450s).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 1607 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Donegal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Red Hugh O'Donnell, Manus O'Donnell, Rory O'Donnell</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tyrconnell, Tír Chonaill, O Donnell</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1054&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tir-chonaill" aria-label="Kingdom of Tir Chonaill on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4501 307 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tir Chonaill lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4821 563L4837 553M4821 563L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4837 553h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4821 563h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4821 563h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Donegal. <a href="/atlas?year=1054&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tir-chonaill">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

